### :::::: builtin-0install: opam upgrade --fixup changes only what the broken dependency needs (#7240)
### <pkg:a.1>
opam-version: "2.0"
depends: "b"
### <pkg:b.1>
opam-version: "2.0"
### <pkg:b.2>
opam-version: "2.0"
### <pkg:c.1>
opam-version: "2.0"
### <pkg:c.2>
opam-version: "2.0"
### opam switch create fixup --empty
### opam install a b.1 c.1
The following actions will be performed:
=== install 3 packages
  - install a 1
  - install b 1
  - install c 1

<><> Processing actions <><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><>
-> installed b.1
-> installed a.1
-> installed c.1
Done.
### :::::: a.1 now requires b >= 2, which the installed b.1 does not satisfy
### <pkg:a.1>
opam-version: "2.0"
depends: "b" {>= "2"}
### OPAMEXTERNALSOLVER=builtin-0install
### opam upgrade --fixup --show
The following actions would be performed:
=== recompile 1 package
  - recompile a 1
=== upgrade 2 packages
  - upgrade   b 1 to 2
  - upgrade   c 1 to 2
